(LINUXCNC DEMO - THE .NGC EXTENSION SELECTS THE LINUXCNC DIALECT)
(THIS CONTROL'S M-CODES ARE SPECIFIED IN THE INTERPRETER ITSELF, NOT)
(ASSIGNED BY A MACHINE BUILDER - SO THE HOVERS HERE ARE EXACT)
(1 DELIBERATE MISTAKE BELOW)

(--- setup: the operator loaded T1 by hand, so tell the control about it ---)
N10 G21 G17 G90 G54
N20 M61 Q1                   (set current tool to 1 with NO tool change)
N30 G0 X0 Y0
N40 G43 H1 Z25.0

(--- M62/M64: the difference that bites you is WHEN they fire ---)
N50 M64 P0                   (dust shoe on - immediately, even during lookahead)
N60 M3 S6000 M8
N70 M62 P1                   (air blast on - queued to fire at THIS point in the path)
N80 G1 Z-2.0 F300.0
N90 G1 X60.0
N100 M63 P1                  (air blast off, also synchronized)
N110 G0 Z25.0

(--- M70/M72: borrow the modal state, then hand it back ---)
N120 M70                     (save motion mode, units, offsets, feed)
N130 G91 G0 X10.0            (work incrementally for a moment)
N140 M72                     (restore - back to G90 without having to re-state it)

(--- M49: hold the programmed feed exactly, knobs ignored ---)
N150 M49
N160 G1 X70.0 F150.0
N170 M48                     (give the operator the override knobs back)

(--- user-defined codes: real numbers, machine-specific meaning ---)
N180 M101 P1                 (runs the 'M101' script in this machine's config)

(--- T2 cuts dry: the coolant rule still works with the bigger table ---)
N190 G0 Z50.0 M5 M9
N200 M6 T2
N210 G0 X20.0 Y20.0
N220 G43 H2 Z25.0            (G0 is still modal here, so this is a rapid)
N230 M3 S3000
N240 G1 Z-1.0 F200.0         (<-- flagged: T2 never turned any coolant on)
N250 M5
N260 G0 Z50.0
N270 M2
